<title>BELGIUM: Belgian bankruptcies fall 7.8 pct in December.</title>
<headline>Belgian bankruptcies fall 7.8 pct in December.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Company bankruptcies in Belgium fell by 44, or 7.8 percent, to 520 in December compared with December 1995, Belgian trade and company data group Infotrade said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It said a total of 7,358 companies went bankrupt in 1996, up 336 or 4.8 percent from 1995.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
